IMPORTANT INTERPRETATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. These standardized trajectories do NOT constitute a composite environmental-pressure index.
2. Z-scores only express departure from each site's own 1900–1919 baseline.
3. A large z-score can occur when baseline variability is small; it must not automatically be interpreted as a proportionally larger ecological effect.
4. Forest-loss pressure is only the sign-reversed standardized forest/natural vegetation trajectory.
5. Correlations among historical variables are descriptive because long-term trends and temporal autocorrelation violate simple independence assumptions.
6. ERSSTv5 is NOT a 70-km buffer measurement. It represents the nearest valid coarse regional SST reconstruction grid cell.
7. ETOPO and Allen Coral Atlas metrics remain separate modern/static ecological-context variables.